<%#
  The title block for a browsing screen. Sits directly under the top bar.

  Locals:
    title:    (required) string or a block-free ERB fragment
    subtitle: (optional) one line under the title
    meta:     (optional) safe HTML rendered as a metadata row under the title
    actions:  (optional) safe HTML for the right-hand side

  A trap worth knowing before you pass `actions:`. The slot is `shrink-0`
  and the title beside it is `flex-1 min-w-0`, so the title can shrink to
  nothing while the actions keep their full width. Whatever fits on that line
  stays on it, and the title is what gives — two buttons were enough to
  squeeze "acme/docs-site" down to one character per line at 390px.

  One action is fine. For two or more, wrap them yourself in a div with a
  phone-width floor (`min-w-80 max-w-80 sm:min-w-0 sm:max-w-xl`), which makes
  the slot too wide to share the line so it wraps under the title instead and
  keeps its own contents on one row. `pull_requests/index` does exactly that
  and explains why in place.
%>
<% title    = local_assigns.fetch(:title) %>
<% subtitle = local_assigns.fetch(:subtitle, nil) %>
<% meta     = local_assigns.fetch(:meta, nil) %>
<% actions  = local_assigns.fetch(:actions, nil) %>

<header class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-4 pb-5 pt-6">
  <div class="min-w-0 flex-1">
    <h1 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold leading-tight tracking-tight text-ink break-words">
      <%= title %>
    </h1>
    <% if subtitle.present? %>
      <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-ink-soft break-words"><%= subtitle %></p>
    <% end %>
    <% if meta.present? %>
      <div class="mt-2 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1.5 text-sm text-ink-soft"><%= meta %></div>
    <% end %>
  </div>
  <% if actions.present? %>
    <div class="flex shrink-0 items-center gap-2"><%= actions %></div>
  <% end %>
</header>
